References: <4F72D447.20004@gmail.com>
 <CAAi6idXZkHR_zNPWAT54iuo3zAxKUJGwb4i_wc=477L6u8o5CQ@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <4F759256.5080308@gmail.com>

There is a new method leslie in FLAdvice that generates a leslie matrix 
based on an FLBRP object e.g,

library(FLAdvice)
library(popbio)

data(ple4)

lmPle4=leslie(FLBRP(ple4))

You can use the popbio package to do all kinds of useful stuff e.g.

# growth rate
log(lambda(lmPle4) )

Laurie



